{"availability":"available","full":"georgekimaninjoroge/Meridian","name":"Meridian","description":"Lightweight, fully-featured, offline-first LMS","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-27T19:31:57Z","updated":"2026-10-17T08:35:12Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://meridianlms.netlify.app","topics":["edtech","firebase","indexeddb","javascript","lms","local-first","low-connectivity","offline-first","postgresql","pwa","service-worker","supabase","vanilla-js"],"demo":"https://meridianlms.netlify.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T21:13:26.838Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T21:13:26.838Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T21:13:26.838Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:51:00.228Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-17T21:13:26.838Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Canvas, Moodle, and Google Classroom share one fatal assumption: the network is always there. The moment it drops, they stop working. No fallback, no queue, no recovery.","For students in Sub-Saharan Africa, Southeast Asia, rural India, and Latin America, that's not an edge case. It's the norm. A student in Nairobi on 3G mid-lecture loses their place. A student in Jakarta when campus WiFi cuts at 8pm loses the session entirely.","Meridian flips the assumption. Offline is the default. Network access is a bonus when available."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/georgekimaninjoroge/Meridian/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1828f200d7e94a72c7229f159501cf9f6fdb0296c05d1736db75c1ebe2b6ab2c","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:00.387Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:00.387Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Canvas, Moodle, and Google Classroom share one fatal assumption: the network is always there. The moment it drops, they stop working. No fallback, no queue, no recovery.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/georgekimaninj